    <p>
      <b>Description</b>
    </p>
    <p>Applies the mathematical function selected by the <code>Function</code> parameter, element-wise, with scalar expansion for vector signals.</p>
    <p>
      <b>Function</b>
    </p>
    <p>Single-input values: <code>exp</code>, <code>log</code>, <code>10^u</code> (10 raised to the input), <code>log10</code>, <code>square</code> (u*u), <code>sqrt</code>, <code>reciprocal</code> (1/u).</p>
    <p>Two-input values (u1 on port 1, u2 on port 2): <code>pow</code> (u1^u2), <code>hypot</code> (sqrt(u1^2+u2^2)), <code>rem</code> (remainder with the sign of u1), <code>mod</code> (modulo with the sign of u2, mod(u1,0)=u1).</p>
    <p>This page describes the native runtime behavior observed in the module C++ sources. Declared phases indicate when the simulation engine calls the block.</p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
